{"resource":{"id":"dbms-learning-roadmap","title":"DBMS \u2014 Learning Roadmap","category":"CS Core","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"10 min","pages":11,"lastUpdated":"May 2026","tags":["DBMS","SQL","Database Systems"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"A structured 12-week roadmap from database fundamentals to advanced DBMS \u2014 with milestones, SQL drills, portfolio projects, certifications, and a career plan."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"prereq","label":"1. Prerequisites"},{"id":"fundamentals","label":"2. Database Fundamentals"},{"id":"sql","label":"3. SQL Basics"},{"id":"design","label":"4. Database Design"},{"id":"rel","label":"5. Relationships"},{"id":"norm","label":"6. Normalization"},{"id":"txn","label":"7. Transactions"},{"id":"idx","label":"8. Indexing"},{"id":"perf","label":"9. Performance Tuning"},{"id":"projects","label":"10. Projects"},{"id":"career","label":"11. Career Preparation"},{"id":"review","label":"Roadmap Review"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"DBMS \u2014 Frequently Asked Questions","tag":"CS Core","time":"9 min"},{"title":"DBMS \u2014 Tips & Tricks","tag":"CS Core","time":"12 min"},{"title":"System Design","tag":"CS Core","time":"20 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Learn DBMS in the correct order \u2014 no gaps, no leapfrogging.</li>\n          <li>Build strong, interview-grade SQL skills.</li>\n          <li>Track weekly milestones and self-check progress.</li>\n          <li>Ship 4 portfolio-ready database projects.</li>\n          <li>Prepare for database-related career paths.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <Figure\n          src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1600&q=80\"\n          caption=\"Roadmap overview \u2014 12 weeks moving from theory \u2192 SQL \u2192 design \u2192 performance \u2192 career.\"\n        />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"prereq\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Prerequisites</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Before starting, you should be comfortable with:</p>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Basic computer literacy and command line.</li>\n          <li>Any one programming language (Python, Java, JS) \u2014 helpful, not mandatory.</li>\n          <li>Set theory intuition (union, intersection).</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"/><path d=\"M9 18h6\"/><path d=\"M10 22h4\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Tooling to install</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">PostgreSQL 16, DBeaver or pgAdmin, VS Code with the SQLTools extension.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"fundamentals\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Database Fundamentals \u2014 Week 1\u20132</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Week n={1} title=\"Concepts\" tasks={[\"Read: DBMS vs file systems\", \"Learn: 3-schema architecture\", \"Draw: your first ER diagram\", \"Milestone: install PostgreSQL and connect via DBeaver\"]} />\n        <Week n={2} title=\"Data models\" tasks={[\"Relational, hierarchical, NoSQL differences\", \"Entities, attributes, relationships\", \"Milestone: model a Library ER diagram (books, members, loans)\"]} />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"sql\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. SQL Basics \u2014 Week 3\u20134</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Week n={3} title=\"DML fundamentals\" tasks={[\"SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, LIMIT\", \"INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE\", \"Aggregations: COUNT, SUM, AVG, GROUP BY, HAVING\", \"Milestone: 50 SQL exercises on a sample DB (LeetCode SQL / HackerRank / pgexercises)\"]} />\n        <Week n={4} title=\"Joins & subqueries\" tasks={[\"INNER / LEFT / RIGHT / FULL joins\", \"Correlated subqueries\", \"CTEs (WITH \u2026)\", \"Window functions: ROW_NUMBER, RANK, LAG, LEAD\"]} />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"design\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Database Design \u2014 Week 5</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Week n={5} title=\"Schema design\" tasks={[\"Naming conventions, surrogate vs natural keys\", \"Data types and defaults\", \"NOT NULL, CHECK, UNIQUE, FK constraints\", \"Milestone: design schema for an e-commerce site (users, products, orders, line items)\"]} />\n        <Figure\n          src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1600&q=80\"\n          caption=\"ER model \u2192 relational schema \u2192 DDL migrations. Design on paper before writing CREATE TABLE.\"\n        />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"rel\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Relationships \u2014 Week 6</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Week n={6} title=\"Cardinality & integrity\" tasks={[\"1:1, 1:N, M:N with join tables\", \"ON DELETE CASCADE vs RESTRICT vs SET NULL\", \"Composite keys in join tables\", \"Milestone: extend e-commerce schema with reviews, categories, tags\"]} />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"norm\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Normalization \u2014 Week 7</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Week n={7} title=\"Normal forms\" tasks={[\"1NF \u2192 2NF \u2192 3NF \u2192 BCNF with examples\", \"Functional dependencies\", \"When to denormalize\", \"Milestone: normalise a messy CSV export to 3NF\"]} />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"txn\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Transactions \u2014 Week 8</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Week n={8} title=\"ACID in practice\" tasks={[\"BEGIN / COMMIT / ROLLBACK / SAVEPOINT\", \"Isolation levels & anomalies\", \"Deadlocks and how DBs resolve them\", \"Milestone: simulate a bank transfer safely under concurrent load\"]} />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"idx\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Indexing \u2014 Week 9</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Week n={9} title=\"B-tree, hash, GIN\" tasks={[\"Single-column vs composite indexes\", \"Covering indexes and index-only scans\", \"EXPLAIN / EXPLAIN ANALYZE\", \"Milestone: take a slow query from 2s to <50ms with the right index\"]} />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"perf\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Performance Tuning \u2014 Week 10</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Week n={10} title=\"Scale reads and writes\" tasks={[\"Query plans, statistics, VACUUM/ANALYZE\", \"Partitioning strategies\", \"Read replicas, connection pooling (PgBouncer)\", \"Introduction to sharding and CAP\"]} />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"projects\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Projects \u2014 Week 11</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Week n={11} title=\"Portfolio builds\" tasks={[\n          \"Project 1: URL shortener \u2014 schema, indexes, analytics\",\n          \"Project 2: Blog CMS \u2014 auth, roles, RLS, tags\",\n          \"Project 3: Inventory manager \u2014 transactions, triggers, audit log\",\n          \"Project 4: Analytics dashboard \u2014 window functions, materialized views\",\n        ]} />\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-amber-500/40 bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"M15 14c.2-1 .7-1.7 1.5-2.5 1-.9 1.5-2.2 1.5-3.5A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .2 2.2 1.5 3.5.7.7 1.3 1.5 1.5 2.5\"/><path d=\"M9 18h6\"/><path d=\"M10 22h4\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Push to GitHub</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Include README with ER diagram, migrations, seed data, and 3 tuned queries with EXPLAIN plans.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"career\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Career Preparation \u2014 Week 12</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Week n={12} title=\"Interview + certs\" tasks={[\n          \"Grind 60 SQL interview problems (LeetCode Hard SQL, StrataScratch)\",\n          \"Rehearse: normalization, ACID, indexing, N+1, deadlocks\",\n          \"Certifications: Oracle SQL Certified, Microsoft DP-300, PostgreSQL Associate (EDB)\",\n          \"Roles to target: SQL Developer, Data Analyst, Backend Engineer, DBA, Data Engineer\",\n        ]} />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"review\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Roadmap Review</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><strong>Progress Tracker:</strong> tick each week only when the milestone is committed to GitHub.</p>\n        <p><strong>Milestones Checklist:</strong> Library ERD \u2705 \u00b7 50 SQL drills \u2705 \u00b7 E-commerce schema \u2705 \u00b7 Normalised CSV \u2705 \u00b7 Concurrent bank transfer \u2705 \u00b7 Query tuned &lt;50ms \u2705 \u00b7 4 portfolio projects \u2705.</p>\n        <p><strong>Career Suggestions:</strong> pair DBMS with either Backend (Node/Java) or Data (Python + dbt) tracks.</p>\n        <p><strong>Next Learning Steps:</strong> Distributed databases, streaming (Kafka + Debezium), warehousing (Snowflake/BigQuery).</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>How many hours per week?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">6\u20138 focused hours. Consistency beats sprints.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Do I need to memorise SQL syntax?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No \u2014 memorise the shape (SELECT/FROM/JOIN/WHERE/GROUP/HAVING/ORDER/LIMIT). Details come with practice.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Should I learn NoSQL alongside?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">After you finish this roadmap. Strong SQL fundamentals make NoSQL much easier.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n          <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n            <li>PostgreSQL Documentation \u2014 postgresql.org/docs</li>\n            <li>MySQL Reference Manual \u2014 dev.mysql.com/doc</li>\n            <li>Oracle Learning \u2014 education.oracle.com</li>\n            <li>Microsoft Learn \u2014 SQL Server & Azure SQL</li>\n            <li>MongoDB University (for NoSQL comparisons)</li>\n            <li>CMU 15-445 Database Systems (open lectures)</li>\n            <li>MIT OpenCourseWare 6.830</li>\n            <li>Silberschatz \u2014 Database System Concepts</li>\n            <li>Elmasri & Navathe \u2014 Fundamentals of Database Systems</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n          This resource is intended for educational purposes only. Information is compiled from official\n          documentation, academic publications, research papers, industry standards, and trusted educational\n          resources. Database technologies, SQL dialects, and best practices evolve over time \u2014 always consult\n          official vendor documentation for the latest information. All trademarks, product names, logos, and\n          intellectual property belong to their respective owners.\n        </p>\n      </div></section>"}